
Contents of "cnet:pfiles/fido/"

    Call_Jam

        - Adds the "CALL" command to CNet. Add this line to the bottom of
          your Menu # 1 (Maintenance Menu) of BBSMENU:

                CALL, CALL jam | {#0pfiles:fido/Call_Jam}
                                 ^
                             Control-Q

        - This command allows you to use the "JamCall.rexx" file from INSIDE
          of CNet. This is great for when you're doing AreaFixes, FREQs, etc
          from other systems.

        - Typed alone, "CALL" will ask you for the needed info, or else you
          can supply it right on the command line, like this:

                Main Prompt> CALL 1:260/121.0 10 30

          This would attempt to dial my bbs(Frontiers) a maximum of 10 times,
          with a 30 "tick" wait between each dial.

        - Check your "poll" log for logged results of this command.


    FidoBusyMessage

        - I run this file in my "sys.welcome" file like this:

                {#0pfiles:fido/FidoBusyMessage}
                ^
            Control-Q

        - This program checks for the existence of any ".PKT" files in your
          INBOUND: directory and if found, will display a message telling
          the user incoming Fido-Net messages are being processed in the
          background. I also have it state that the SPEED of the system may
          be comprimised until these messages are finished being processed,
          so if you're running on a faster CPU, you may need to reword what
          this file will tell the users.


    NetLogViewer

        - Add the following line to Menu # 1 (Maintenance Menu) of BBSMENU:

                NL, Net Log | {#0pfiles:fido/NetLogViewer}
                              ^
                          Control-Q

        - Gives you an easy way to view and/or delete log files used when
          running networks. Currently set up to display these logs, which
          MAY or MAY NOT need to be changed for your uses:

                JamMail.log, TrapList, Toss, Poll, FreqMate


    NetUtils

        - Add following line to Menu # 1 (Maintenance Menu) of BBSMENU:

                NET, NET utils | {#0pfiles:fido/NetUtils}
                                 ^
                             Control-Q

        - Gives you the following utilities:

                1. Net Logs          (Uses NL command above)
                2. Get Node Info     (Uses GetNode   in "mail:fido/")
                3. List Net Names    (Uses ENumNet   in "mail:fido/")
                4. List  Accounting  (Uses ListAcct  in "mail:fido/")
                5. Clear Accounting  (Uses ClearAcct in "mail:fido/")


